# Shell scripts are checked out LF on every platform.
#
# The launchers run on Linux - the team box, and the VM a paid run uses -
# but this repository is also worked on from Windows, where git's default
# `core.autocrlf` rewrites them on checkout. bash does not strip the
# carriage return: it reads the shebang as `/usr/bin/env bash\r` and the
# run dies with `bad interpreter: no such file or directory`, which names
# a file that plainly exists and sends the reader looking in the wrong
# place entirely.
#
# Scoped to *.sh on purpose. A blanket `* text=auto` would renormalise the
# whole tree the next time anybody touches it, and a diff that large buries
# whatever change it travelled with.
*.sh text eol=lf
